1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:13,619
Catherine Adeyemi refused the therapy in twenty
forty-nine, and again in fifty-four, and

2
00:00:13,639 --> 00:00:19,260
again in sixty-one, and the last time they
discussed it she was seventy-three and she

3
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:25,100
put her hand on his arm, which she had never done in
twenty-two years, and said: Albert,

4
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,958
I would like to be finished.

5
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:33,990
She retired in twenty sixty-two, at seventy-four, after
thirty-five years as chief financial

6
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:40,048
officer. She was the last of them. Dana Whitfield
had died in twenty forty-four. Tomás

7
00:00:40,068 --> 00:00:46,318
Reyes had taken the therapy and then, in twenty
fifty-eight, at sixty, had stopped taking

8
00:00:46,338 --> 00:00:52,377
it, quietly, without telling anyone, and had lived
four more years and died in a house

9
00:00:52,397 --> 00:00:54,984
on the Brandywine with the sound off.

10
00:00:55,552 --> 00:01:01,437
She bought a house in County Clare, on a hillside
above the Atlantic, four hundred miles

11
00:01:01,457 --> 00:01:07,342
from the nearest Umbrella facility, and she read, and
she walked, and for the first time

12
00:01:07,362 --> 00:01:11,703
in her adult life she was bored, and she
found that she liked it.

13
00:01:14,274 --> 00:01:19,883
He came every year. Not on a schedule; she would not
have tolerated a schedule. He would

14
00:01:19,903 --> 00:01:25,512
simply be there, in the lane, in a long black coat,
on some afternoon in the autumn, and

15
00:01:25,532 --> 00:01:31,269
she would put the kettle on and complain about the
drive, and they would sit by the window

16
00:01:31,289 --> 00:01:35,427
and argue for four hours about something
that no longer mattered.

17
00:01:35,998 --> 00:01:41,798
In twenty seventy-three she was eighty-five and
dying of an ordinary thing that could

18
00:01:41,818 --> 00:01:46,387
have been fixed in an afternoon by a
medicine her own company made.

19
00:01:48,575 --> 00:01:49,703
Don't say it.

20
00:01:50,224 --> 00:01:51,568
I haven't said anything.

21
00:01:52,087 --> 00:01:56,219
You're about to. You're going to tell me there's an
infusion, and that it would take an

22
00:01:56,239 --> 00:01:58,318
hour, and that I'd have another
forty years.

23
00:01:58,837 --> 00:01:59,578
Sixty.

24
00:02:00,099 --> 00:02:01,359
Sixty. God.

25
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:07,439
She was quiet for a while. The light
moved on the wall.

26
00:02:08,129 --> 00:02:09,453
Do you know why not?

27
00:02:09,973 --> 00:02:13,537
Tell me. I've had forty years to guess
and I've never been sure.

28
00:02:15,557 --> 00:02:19,902
Because everyone who takes it belongs to you. Not
because you make them. Because they

29
00:02:19,922 --> 00:02:24,318
know who made it, and because they'd have died
without it, and after a while that gets

30
00:02:24,338 --> 00:02:28,888
into the floor of a person and they stop being able
to tell where you end and they begin.

31
00:02:29,288 --> 00:02:33,845
I've watched it happen to eleven billion people. I
watched it happen to Owen Carrick,

32
00:02:33,865 --> 00:02:38,584
who spent sixteen years trying to put you in prison
and took it in twenty forty-one like

33
00:02:38,604 --> 00:02:39,337
everyone else.

34
00:02:40,739 --> 00:02:45,063
I'm the last person alive who remembers what you
looked like when you were small enough

35
00:02:45,083 --> 00:02:47,311
to be stopped. I'd like to take
that with me.

36
00:02:50,330 --> 00:02:55,415
He did not argue. That was the thing she noticed,
and thought about that night when she

37
00:02:55,435 --> 00:02:58,231
could not sleep, and never got to
ask him about.

38
00:02:58,801 --> 00:03:04,022
In twenty twenty-eight, in a glass office in
Manhattan, he would have argued. He would

39
00:03:04,042 --> 00:03:09,202
have found the four sentences that turned her,
because he could always find them, and

40
00:03:09,222 --> 00:03:12,370
she would have taken the infusion
and been grateful.

41
00:03:12,941 --> 00:03:19,012
He sat in a small chair in a small room in Ireland
and let an eighty-five-year-old woman

42
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:24,965
tell him that she was dying in order to not belong
to him, and he did not say one word

43
00:03:24,985 --> 00:03:25,795
to stop her.

44
00:03:28,485 --> 00:03:31,824
Can I ask you something? The real one.
The one I've never asked.

45
00:03:32,344 --> 00:03:32,984
Yes.

46
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:38,199
In twenty twenty-eight you told me there was a
facility under the old building. You told

47
00:03:38,219 --> 00:03:42,913
me it was legal the way the Manhattan Project was
legal. I asked you if anyone was being

48
00:03:42,933 --> 00:03:47,627
hurt and you said no, and it was true, and I've
thought about that answer for forty-five

49
00:03:47,647 --> 00:03:47,948
years.

50
00:03:49,348 --> 00:03:54,102
If I had asked you the same question in twenty
thirty-six — after Pale Horse — what would

51
00:03:54,122 --> 00:03:54,852
you have said?

52
00:03:57,872 --> 00:04:00,732
He looked out of the window at the
sea for a long time.

53
00:04:01,423 --> 00:04:02,447
I'd have said no.

54
00:04:02,967 --> 00:04:04,601
And it would have been a lie.

55
00:04:05,122 --> 00:04:05,762
Yes.

56
00:04:07,782 --> 00:04:08,969
Thank you.

57
00:04:11,489 --> 00:04:17,486
She died four days later, in the afternoon, in the
chair by the window, with a book she

58
00:04:17,506 --> 00:04:18,870
had read four times.

59
00:04:19,439 --> 00:04:25,542
She had eleven billion dollars, and no children, and a
will of four pages that left almost

60
00:04:25,562 --> 00:04:31,324
all of it to an endowment for the audit of public
institutions, in perpetuity, with a

61
00:04:31,344 --> 00:04:37,106
clause — drafted by her, and by the finest legal
minds money could buy, and upheld in

62
00:04:37,126 --> 00:04:42,888
every jurisdiction it was ever tested in — that no
entity controlled by or affiliated

63
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:48,874
with Umbrella Life Sciences, or its successors, could
ever sit on its board, receive its

64
00:04:48,894 --> 00:04:50,711
funds, or see its accounts.

65
00:04:51,279 --> 00:04:57,204
It is still operating. It has audited the
Directorate nineteen times. It has never once

66
00:04:57,224 --> 00:04:58,912
been permitted to finish.

67
00:05:01,983 --> 00:05:07,947
He came to the funeral. There were fourteen people.
Nobody there had any idea who he was,

68
00:05:07,967 --> 00:05:12,857
which he had arranged, and which was the last
favour he ever did for her.

69
00:05:14,927 --> 00:05:20,642
He flew back to Arklay that night. He had buried the
last person alive who had known him

70
00:05:20,662 --> 00:05:26,183
before the emblem went up on the tower, and he had,
so far as he could see, centuries

71
00:05:26,203 --> 00:05:31,984
of administration in front of him, and nothing in the
sky that he had not already priced.

72
00:05:32,553 --> 00:05:34,387
That lasted eleven months.

73
00:05:37,958 --> 00:05:43,123
The thing that had been working out there came into
the solar system in the autumn of

74
00:05:43,143 --> 00:05:47,759
twenty seventy-four, and it did not come
quietly, and it did not come alone.

75
00:05:48,329 --> 00:05:54,066
There were nine of them. They crossed the heliopause
at a velocity that the Directorate's

76
00:05:54,086 --> 00:05:59,694
astronomers spent four days refusing to publish,
because publishing it would have meant

77
00:05:59,714 --> 00:06:05,193
admitting that the objects had decelerated from a
substantial fraction of light speed

78
00:06:05,213 --> 00:06:09,269
without radiating the energy that such a
deceleration requires.

79
00:06:09,838 --> 00:06:15,740
They took up a formation at forty-one astronomical
units, beyond the orbit of Neptune,

80
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:18,081
and they stopped, and they waited.

81
00:06:20,151 --> 00:06:26,285
And then, eleven days later, they transmitted. In
four hundred and six human languages,

82
00:06:26,305 --> 00:06:32,298
including nineteen that had been extinct for a
century, and one that had been extinct

83
00:06:32,318 --> 00:06:37,391
for four thousand years and was known to
about thirty scholars on Earth.

84
00:06:37,961 --> 00:06:44,056
The message was four sentences long. It has been
reprinted more times than any text in

85
00:06:44,076 --> 00:06:45,834
human history except one.

86
00:06:48,024 --> 00:06:52,366
We have listened for one hundred and forty of your
years. We are the Tollhouse Compact.

87
00:06:52,386 --> 00:06:56,628
We buy, we sell, and we do not make war upon
markets. Name one who may speak for your

88
00:06:56,648 --> 00:06:59,838
world, and we will come to the third
planet and open an account.

89
00:07:02,858 --> 00:07:08,864
The species had four weeks to decide who spoke for
it. It spent nineteen days arguing,

90
00:07:08,884 --> 00:07:13,629
which the Director considered, privately, a
triumph of self-control.

91
00:07:14,197 --> 00:07:20,024
There were four positions. The United Nations argued
that the Secretary-General should

92
00:07:20,044 --> 00:07:25,870
speak, as the only officeholder elected by the whole
of the species, in the sense that

93
00:07:25,890 --> 00:07:31,784
a hundred and ninety-three governments had voted for
him. The largest states argued for

94
00:07:31,804 --> 00:07:37,970
a council of the largest states. A coalition of forty
smaller nations argued for a lottery.

95
00:07:37,990 --> 00:07:43,952
And a very great many people, in every country on
Earth, said the obvious thing out loud

96
00:07:43,972 --> 00:07:48,778
on the internet within about four hours of
the message being published.

97
00:07:49,348 --> 00:07:51,593
Name one who may speak for your world.

98
00:07:52,163 --> 00:07:57,736
It was not even a debate in the end. It was a fact
that had been true since Geneva in

99
00:07:57,756 --> 00:08:02,539
twenty forty-seven and had simply never been
stated in a single sentence.

100
00:08:03,108 --> 00:08:09,335
On the fourth of November, twenty seventy-four, the
Accord Council voted by a hundred

101
00:08:09,355 --> 00:08:15,581
and thirty-one to ten to designate the Director of
Umbrella Life Sciences as the sole

102
00:08:15,601 --> 00:08:20,283
representative of the human species for
the purposes of contact.

103
00:08:20,853 --> 00:08:27,503
Ten votes against. He remembered all ten. Not with
anger — with something closer to fondness.

104
00:08:27,523 --> 00:08:28,651
Somebody had to.

105
00:08:31,221 --> 00:08:36,936
One of the nine came in to Earth orbit, and it was
eleven kilometres long, and it took

106
00:08:36,956 --> 00:08:42,871
station four hundred kilometres above the Pacific,
and it did nothing threatening at all,

107
00:08:42,891 --> 00:08:48,940
and every seismograph on the planet recorded the day
it arrived because four billion people

108
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:49,873
moved at once.

109
00:08:50,443 --> 00:08:56,128
He went up to it in the Wilmington, which was by then
one of four void-cutters, and which

110
00:08:56,148 --> 00:09:01,641
he had ordered to stand off at nine thousand
kilometres with its weapons cold, because

111
00:09:01,661 --> 00:09:07,282
he had spent forty-eight years learning that the
first move of a negotiation is the only

112
00:09:07,302 --> 00:09:08,949
one you get to make twice.

113
00:09:09,519 --> 00:09:13,819
He went across in a shuttle, with nine
people. Four of them were human.

114
00:09:16,389 --> 00:09:22,764
The chamber they were received in was designed, he
understood immediately, to be overwhelming.

115
00:09:22,784 --> 00:09:28,752
It was four hundred metres across and it held
representatives of eleven species, and the

116
00:09:28,772 --> 00:09:34,671
light in it moved, and the air smelled of something
between cinnamon and ozone, and the

117
00:09:34,691 --> 00:09:38,278
gravity was not quite Earth's and
not quite constant.

118
00:09:38,847 --> 00:09:45,155
Every single element of it was a negotiating position.
He recognised the technique perfectly.

119
00:09:45,175 --> 00:09:48,692
He had once made a landlord walk
through a basement.

120
00:09:50,763 --> 00:09:56,374
The being that spoke for the Tollhouse Compact was
called — as near as the translation

121
00:09:56,394 --> 00:10:01,939
ever got — the Broker. It was four metres tall and
very thin, and it had no face that

122
00:10:01,959 --> 00:10:07,178
a human being could read, and it spoke English
with the warmth of a good doctor.

123
00:10:07,869 --> 00:10:12,705
Director. Welcome. You are the two hundred and
eleventh species we have opened an account

124
00:10:12,725 --> 00:10:14,833
with. May I tell you how this proceeds?

125
00:10:15,351 --> 00:10:15,992
Please.

126
00:10:16,514 --> 00:10:20,575
We buy. Your world produces four things of interest
to the Compact, three of which you

127
00:10:20,595 --> 00:10:24,989
do not presently value. We will pay well. In exchange
we sell: medicine beyond your medicine,

128
00:10:25,009 --> 00:10:29,070
power beyond your power, and passage. Within forty
of your years you will be a wealthy

129
00:10:29,090 --> 00:10:33,152
species. Within four hundred you will be a member in
good standing. We ask nothing but

130
00:10:33,172 --> 00:10:33,722
the account.

131
00:10:35,741 --> 00:10:36,660
And the terms?

132
00:10:37,179 --> 00:10:42,312
Standard. Exclusivity of trade. Non-development of
certain technologies, which are listed.

133
00:10:42,332 --> 00:10:47,635
Non-expansion beyond your system for one hundred years,
after which the boundary is reviewed.

134
00:10:47,655 --> 00:10:49,066
And the customary surety.

135
00:10:49,587 --> 00:10:50,336
Which is?

136
00:10:51,855 --> 00:10:57,753
A registered claim over the system itself. It is a
formality. It has never once been exercised

137
00:10:57,773 --> 00:10:59,201
in nine thousand years.

138
00:11:01,721 --> 00:11:03,625
He did not answer for a while.

139
00:11:04,193 --> 00:11:09,899
He had, by then, spent forty-eight years reading rooms
full of people who wanted something

140
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:15,306
from him, and it turned out that the skill
transferred, because the Broker's body had

141
00:11:15,326 --> 00:11:21,032
a posture and its posture had a grammar, and the
grammar said: this has worked two hundred

142
00:11:21,052 --> 00:11:21,923
and ten times.

143
00:11:22,494 --> 00:11:28,758
In the Thought Acceleration — which was, by twenty
seventy-four, running at four thousand

144
00:11:28,778 --> 00:11:34,690
to one, in nine parallel threads — he took a
subjective afternoon to think about it.

145
00:11:35,259 --> 00:11:40,619
He thought about a licence agreement with the word
non-exclusive on page three, and a

146
00:11:40,639 --> 00:11:46,062
landlord who had not read section nine, and a board
of directors who had not read page

147
00:11:46,082 --> 00:11:51,569
eleven. He thought about how you take a thing from
people who believe they are the ones

148
00:11:51,589 --> 00:11:57,202
doing the taking, and he recognised, in every line of
the Broker's offer, the exact shape

149
00:11:57,222 --> 00:11:58,214
of his own work.

150
00:11:58,784 --> 00:12:02,583
Then he came back, and it had been a fifth
of a second, and he said:

151
00:12:04,774 --> 00:12:05,394
No.

152
00:12:08,413 --> 00:12:10,937
I do not think you understand the offer.

153
00:12:11,457 --> 00:12:17,046
I understand it perfectly. You've made it two hundred
and ten times. Let me tell you what

154
00:12:17,066 --> 00:12:17,424
it is.

155
00:12:18,825 --> 00:12:23,693
You will pay us handsomely for four things, three of
which we do not know the value of,

156
00:12:23,713 --> 00:12:28,582
which means you will pay us a fraction of what they
are worth and we will be delighted,

157
00:12:28,602 --> 00:12:33,358
because we have nothing to compare it to. You will
sell us medicine and power, and in

158
00:12:33,378 --> 00:12:38,303
forty years we will be unable to manufacture either
for ourselves, because why would we,

159
00:12:38,323 --> 00:12:43,136
when you sell it so cheaply. The non-development
list is not a safety measure; it is a

160
00:12:43,156 --> 00:12:48,081
list of every technology by which a client stops
being a client. And the surety over our

161
00:12:48,101 --> 00:12:52,857
system is a formality that has never been exercised
because it has never needed to be

162
00:12:52,877 --> 00:12:57,746
— because by the time exercising it would be worth
your while, no species has ever been

163
00:12:57,766 --> 00:12:59,151
in a condition to object.

164
00:13:01,051 --> 00:13:06,617
You are not offering us an account. You are offering
us dependency, on a schedule, with

165
00:13:06,637 --> 00:13:08,736
a lien on our home as collateral.

166
00:13:11,256 --> 00:13:17,436
The chamber did something. It was not a sound. The
light in it changed, slightly, in a

167
00:13:17,456 --> 00:13:21,690
way that eleven species understood and
four humans did not.

168
00:13:22,379 --> 00:13:25,356
That is an unusually complete reading.

169
00:13:25,876 --> 00:13:32,067
I've made the same offer myself. Forty years ago, to a
landlord in Delaware, for a building.

170
00:13:32,087 --> 00:13:33,552
It worked beautifully.

171
00:13:36,072 --> 00:13:41,319
Then you will understand that refusal has a cost. The
Compact does not make war on markets.

172
00:13:41,339 --> 00:13:46,470
But a world that declines the account is not a
market. It is a curiosity. And curiosities

173
00:13:46,490 --> 00:13:47,744
are visited by others.

174
00:13:48,263 --> 00:13:48,840
Who?

175
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:53,256
The Veth Hegemony is nine hundred light years from
your star and has been informed of

176
00:13:53,276 --> 00:13:57,218
your existence since your first radio. They do not
buy. They do not sell. They arrive,

177
00:13:57,238 --> 00:14:01,180
and they assess, and what they find useful they
administer, and what they find useless

178
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:05,188
they clear. We are, Director, the only wall between
your species and that. That is what

179
00:14:05,208 --> 00:14:09,149
you are actually being offered, and that is why two
hundred and ten species have taken

180
00:14:09,169 --> 00:14:09,288
it.

181
00:14:11,807 --> 00:14:18,240
And that — the Directorate's analysts would conclude,
over the following nine years, reading

182
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:24,272
the transcript four thousand times — was the only
genuinely honest sentence the Broker

183
00:14:24,292 --> 00:14:25,254
spoke all day.

184
00:14:27,325 --> 00:14:32,794
He took off his sunglasses. He had thought about it
in the shuttle, and had decided it

185
00:14:32,814 --> 00:14:38,284
was probably meaningless to a species with no faces,
and did it anyway, because it was

186
00:14:38,304 --> 00:14:39,497
not for the Broker.

187
00:14:40,187 --> 00:14:44,729
Then let me make a counter-offer, and let me be
as honest as you have just been.

188
00:14:45,129 --> 00:14:49,350
We will not take your account. We will buy from you,
at market, in cash, and we will sell

189
00:14:49,370 --> 00:14:53,401
to you, at market, and we will reverse-engineer
every single thing you sell us, which

190
00:14:53,421 --> 00:14:57,498
you know we will do, and which your non-development
list exists to prevent. We will do

191
00:14:57,518 --> 00:15:01,596
it anyway. We will be the two hundred and eleventh
species to say no, and probably the

192
00:15:01,616 --> 00:15:03,741
first, and you will find it
very interesting.

193
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:07,424
And when the Veth come, we will
deal with the Veth.

194
00:15:09,945 --> 00:15:11,721
You have four ships.

195
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:14,097
I have had four of something before.

196
00:15:17,118 --> 00:15:23,090
The nine vessels left the solar system in January of
twenty seventy-five. They did not

197
00:15:23,110 --> 00:15:29,431
threaten. They did not retaliate. The Compact had not
made war on a market in nine thousand

198
00:15:29,451 --> 00:15:35,633
years, and a species that had declined the account
was not a market, and they had a great

199
00:15:35,653 --> 00:15:36,748
deal else to do.

200
00:15:37,317 --> 00:15:43,648
Before they went, the Broker sent one final private
transmission, addressed to the Director

201
00:15:43,668 --> 00:15:49,649
personally, in a language that the Farside Array
took four years to confirm was one of

202
00:15:49,669 --> 00:15:55,720
the Compact's internal trade dialects and not, as
had initially been assumed, an error.

203
00:15:56,289 --> 00:16:02,648
It was eleven words long. The Directorate has never
published it. It is, however, carved

204
00:16:02,668 --> 00:16:09,461
— in the original characters, untranslated — above the
door of a room on Arklay Free Territory

205
00:16:09,481 --> 00:16:11,997
that the public is not admitted to.

206
00:16:14,187 --> 00:16:17,820
We have met your kind before. We did
not like them either.

207
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:24,936
He stood on the bridge of the
Wilmington and watched them go.

208
00:16:25,504 --> 00:16:31,688
For forty-eight years he had been the most dangerous
thing in every room he had ever entered.

209
00:16:31,708 --> 00:16:37,424
He had woken in a chair in the rain with a virus in
his blood and a machine in the air

210
00:16:37,444 --> 00:16:43,361
and had never, in half a century, met anything that
could not be out-thought, out-waited,

211
00:16:43,381 --> 00:16:44,294
or out-bought.

212
00:16:44,865 --> 00:16:50,419
And a four-metre creature with no face had just
told him, courteously, that there was

213
00:16:50,439 --> 00:16:55,994
something nine hundred light years away that
arrived, and assessed, and cleared — and

214
00:16:56,014 --> 00:17:01,766
that the only reason it had not arrived already was
that a trading company had found his

215
00:17:01,786 --> 00:17:05,570
species more profitable as a customer
than as a clearance.

216
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:11,292
He found, standing on the bridge,
that he was not afraid.

217
00:17:11,861 --> 00:17:17,672
He examined that carefully, because it was strange,
and because forty-eight years of being

218
00:17:17,692 --> 00:17:23,503
right had taught him to be suspicious of his own calm.
He was not afraid. He was something

219
00:17:23,523 --> 00:17:29,011
else, and it took him a subjective hour in the
Thought Acceleration to find the word,

220
00:17:29,031 --> 00:17:31,603
and when he found it he did not like it.

221
00:17:33,673 --> 00:17:34,930
He was relieved.

222
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:40,991
For twenty-seven years he had owned a species. There
had been nothing left to take. He

223
00:17:41,011 --> 00:17:46,503
had built the thing he had spent two lifetimes
wanting, and it had been finished for a

224
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:51,950
decade, and the ruling of it was administration —
councils, and quotas, and a hundred

225
00:17:51,970 --> 00:17:54,835
and forty-one governments that
never said no.

226
00:17:55,404 --> 00:18:00,737
And somewhere nine hundred light years away there
was an empire that had never heard of

227
00:18:00,757 --> 00:18:00,983
him.

228
00:18:03,673 --> 00:18:04,570
There you are.

229
00:18:06,590 --> 00:18:12,163
There was nobody in his head to answer. He had
stopped noticing that a long time ago.

230
00:18:12,732 --> 00:18:18,202
But if the old voice had still been there — if the
thing that had argued with him in a

231
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:23,884
thousand cars, and wept on a balcony, and admitted
once, on a terrace above the Atlantic,

232
00:18:23,904 --> 00:18:29,374
that it had been wrong about everything except the
goal — if it had been there to hear

233
00:18:29,394 --> 00:18:33,076
him say it, it would have recognised
the tone immediately.

234
00:18:33,646 --> 00:18:39,221
It was the tone of a man who has just been told
that the war is not over after all.
